Q1. Basic Operations Program
a = 10
b = 3

print("Addition:", a + b)
print("Subtraction:", a - b)
print("Multiplication:", a * b)
print("Division:", a / b)
print("Floor division:", a // b)
print("Modulus:", a % b)
print("Exponentiation:", a ** b)


Q2. Output Prediction & Operator Explanation
Output:
3.4
3
2
289
Operator Differences:
●	/ (Division): Performs standard division and returns a float result (17 / 5 = 3.4).
●	// (Floor Division): Divides and rounds down to the nearest whole integer (17 // 5 = 3).
●	% (Modulus): Calculates the remainder after division (17 % 5 = 2).


